        "procedure": "Under aerobic conditions, Dy(NO3)3·5H2O (0.0343 g, 0.075 mmol), di-2-pyridyl ketone (0.0138 g, 0.075 mmol), HL (0.0112 g, 0.0375 mmol), NaN3 (0.0060 g, 0.092 mmol) and triethylamine (0.0228 g, 0.225 mmol) were stirred in methanol (20 mL) for 2 h to give a bright yellow solution, which was filtered. Yellow crystals formed by slow evaporation over about 15 days and were collected by filtration. HL = 2-(benzothiazol-2-yl-hydrazonomethyl)-6-methoxyphenol, prepared by a reported method.",
